<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="yellow">Honed Edge</ansi> (enchantment)

Honed Edge is a beginner enchantment that sharpens a weapon beyond what
any whetstone could achieve. The mutation bonds with the blade's edge,
maintaining an impossibly fine cutting line at the cost of a small
portion of your life force.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Recipe ━━━</ansi>

  Skill:       <ansi fg="skill">enchanting</ansi> 0 (no minimum)
  Station:     <ansi fg="yellow">enchanting_circle</ansi>
  Ingredients: 1x binding-paste, 1x healers-root
  Target:      Any weapon in your inventory
  Time:        3 rounds

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Enchantment Tiers ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Tier 0 — Keen</ansi>
  A subtle improvement to the weapon's edge. Increases damage slightly.
  Reserves 1% of your health pool.
  "The edge holds an unusually sharp line."

  <ansi fg="yellow">Tier 1 — Razor-Edged</ansi>
  The bond deepens and the edge becomes unnaturally sharp. Greater damage
  bonus. Reserves 2% of your health pool.
  "The blade's edge gleams with unnatural sharpness."

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ How It Works ━━━</ansi>

Craft the enchantment at an enchanting circle with the required materials
and a weapon in your inventory. Once applied, the weapon begins at Tier 0.
As you use the weapon in combat, the enchantment grows stronger and may
advance to the next tier over time.

The enchantment reserves a portion of your health — you will see a dark
section in your health bar representing the energy claimed by the bond.

